 - `Schedule.week(therapist, monday)` returns a therapist's non-cancelled appointments for the week as a dict keyed by each date (all seven days, empty lists included), sorted by start time.
 - New client register in `clients.py`: `Client` dataclass and `ClientBook` with `add(client)` and `find_by_phone(phone)`. Phone numbers are normalized, so `079 123 45 67`, `+41 79 123 45 67` and `0041791234567` all find the same client. Adding a phone number that is already registered raises `ValueError`.
 - `ClientBook.search(text)` returns clients whose name contains `text`, ignoring case, in the order they were added; a blank query returns `[]`.
+- `Schedule.is_fully_booked(therapist, day)` is true when no treatment (even the shortest) fits in the therapist's free time on `day`, counting turnaround gaps; a closed day also counts as fully booked, so the booking page can grey it out.
 
